{"id": "EUVD-2026-82212", "enisaUuid": "2e38dca1-6455-3e96-a57f-7cf026c10752", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rvt: Return NULL after port allocation failure\n\nrvt_alloc_device() deallocates the IB device when its port array cannot\nbe allocated but then returns the pointer to the released allocation.\nCallers treat any non-NULL value as valid and dereference it, resulting\nin a use-after-free.\n\nReturn NULL immediately after deallocation so callers can propagate the\nallocation failure.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7129930d1ec46c03a0de07fdce6c29f75795006", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a1a7a5e2fe1a15824fa9ae5edd8f008259471d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80968b42d13080bf7bc1f3ee17fef126ce2ad98f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1e1b25723af44328524c7b54433e4bf0ab9930c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2982eaf3b9d2d953318c74cd6f1b7576ea6d7b1f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wqhx-qpfw-hj6x", "CVE-2026-93104"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0802b0a7-b7e5-33f7-b8d2-06b04709aec2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "446d58db-0736-39f4-aefe-698679f4992b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff6acd69518e0a84bd9c9b7f1bd4313f7076db97 <b7129930d1ec46c03a0de07fdce6c29f75795006"}, {"id": "4a8041ff-7edd-32d2-9ae1-cd51376a9bb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff6acd69518e0a84bd9c9b7f1bd4313f7076db97 <2982eaf3b9d2d953318c74cd6f1b7576ea6d7b1f"}, {"id": "537e1e41-fc50-3e88-8655-d68aa0530aaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff6acd69518e0a84bd9c9b7f1bd4313f7076db97 <b1e1b25723af44328524c7b54433e4bf0ab9930c"}, {"id": "5a25c626-8bd3-3b8b-88ab-d1fb6662954b", "product": {"nam